Do you enjoy working with your hands and are you comfortable with precise, repetitive work? Would you like to work with equipment that is essential for aviation safety? Are you looking for a job where you’ll be hired directly by the company? Then this position in Duiven might be a great opportunity for you.

What are you going to do?
As a production worker, you’ll help inspect and test safety equipment for aircraft. Your work ensures that critical safety products meet strict aviation standards before they are returned to airlines. You will follow clear, step-by-step instructions written in English. The job requires accuracy, attention to detail, and the ability to follow procedures carefully. Your daily tasks may include:

- Inspecting aviation safety products according to established procedures;
- Checking seams, materials, and joints for damage or wear;
- Conducting inspections, pressure tests, and inflating emergency slides;
- Recording inspection results in the company system;
- Working closely with colleagues from various departments.

This position involves repetitive tasks, so it’s important that you enjoy structured work. This is a full-time position (40 hours) Monday through Friday, from 7:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. In the future, the company may implement a two-shift system, so flexibility is appreciated.

What do we offer?
- You will be hired directly by the company;
- Salary between €2,900 and €3,600 gross per month;
- A great bonus plan;
- A detailed training period of several months;
- Stable working hours and a structured environment;
- Travel allowance;
- A friendly team where colleagues know each other well;
- Opportunities to learn multiple departments over time.

